            "review_title": "Review at Sorrento Restaurant & Bar",
            "review_text": "Tristan B\n8 contributions\n0\nVery poor organisation and customer service\nJan 2026 • Couples\nWe visited Sorrento two nights ago for cocktails and a light lunch. The views were unbelievable and the service was decent, so we decided to book a table for today (Saturday) at 5:30pm, specifically requesting a seat down by the water for my partner’s birthday. The waiter confirmed the booking, and I even wrote the table request in Vietnamese so there would be no misunderstanding.\n\nWhen we arrived on time, it looked like the entire restaurant had been booked out for an event — yet the exact tables by the water that we reserved were completely free. The waiter repeatedly told us there was space upstairs, but the only reason we booked this restaurant again was for the waterfront seating. If these tables weren’t available, the booking shouldn’t have been taken.\n\nAfter insisting that we had booked downstairs, the waiter laughed and said “yes, ok,” but then left us sitting there with no further contact for about 15 minutes. We obviously left at that point.\n\nIt’s such a shame because the place is genuinely beautiful, and our first experience a couple of days ago was perfect. The owners really need to speak with their younger staff and remind them that customers should be treated with respect and fairness. A great location doesn’t excuse poor service.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten January 24, 2026",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-10",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
